 ## Overview
-Block face vertex layout defines the static geometric primitives for a unit cube, serving as the fundamental mesh template for blocky meshing algorithms [S1, unofficial]. It specifies the positions, colors, and texture coordinates for the six faces of a cube, allowing surface extraction methods to generate meshes by instantiating these faces for visible voxel boundaries [S2, unofficial]. It differs from sibling methods like [Greedy Meshing](1776-greedy-meshing.md) or [Boolean Voxel Meshing](971-boolean-voxel-meshing.md) by providing only the raw vertex data for individual faces without performing topology optimization, face culling, or merging of adjacent coplanar faces [G].
