 ## How it works
-The method constructs a unit cube mesh centered at the origin or defined in local space, consisting of 6 faces [S1, unofficial]. Each face is composed of 2 triangles, resulting in 6 vertices per face and 36 vertices total for the complete cube [S2, unofficial]. The layout supports instanced rendering where the base geometry is constant, and instance attributes (position, color, texture index) vary per voxel [G].
